# Deep Audit — Manual Rule

Pull this in with `@910-deep-audit` when running Gate 4. Full standard: @law/AUDIT_SIX_POSTURE.md

All six postures. Every modified and new file. No scope-narrowing. **Time is never the constraint.**

## Posture 1 — STRUCTURAL
Every file in "Files Touched" actually touched; every file in "Files NOT Touched" actually
untouched — verified, not assumed. Line counts, hashes, workspace integrity, no foreign artifacts.
Every claim in the delivery note checked against source.
`git diff --stat` · `git status --porcelain` · `wc -l` · `md5sum` · `rg`

## Posture 2 — BEHAVIORAL
Trace every new execution path end to end. Every catch block examined — an empty catch is a red
flag, always. Idempotency on state mutation. Cross-store contracts checked for partial-state
failure. Signature changed → **every** call site confirmed, not most.

## Posture 3 — ADVERSARIAL
Read cold. No carryover trust. Every statement in the brief is an assertion to verify; a prior
PASS is a claim, not permission. **The cleaner the report, the harder you read.**

## Posture 4 — WHOLE-APP SECURITY
Not scoped to the delta. Secrets not in source, logs, commits, or context. Encryption intact. No
sensitive data in plaintext storage. Input validated at boundaries. No debug affordance shipping.

## Posture 5 — FUTURE-READER
Read every doc change as a stranger, and as David five years from now. Drift between docs and
source. Anything that only makes sense if you were in the room.

## Posture 6 — SYNTHESIS
Check against known-deferred items in `state/RISKS.md` and `state/TODO.md`. Deferred item gotten
worse → escalate. New finding duplicates a known-deferred one → note it, move on, do not re-flag.

## Output

Use @harness/templates/AUDIT_REPORT.md. Severity: **Blocker** (back to G3) / **Warning** / **Note**.

Label honestly: any posture skipped or file excluded → it is a **partial** audit and says so.
Built it yourself → **"self-audit — not independent."** Language drift is itself a finding.
